    {
      "_id": "1d8c7152a5ed1ae0",
      "name": "AN/EDQ-12 ANDREWS",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>The Air Defense Naval Directed Energy Weapons System: a particle beam that fries an incoming missile's control circuits (it veers off target — Area-Effect Scatter, Rigger 2 p.60, if you like) or detonates it in flight, equally likely at the gamemaster's call. It also engages aircraft, and fits only nuclear-powered ships.</p><table><tr><th>Type</th><td>L-ATGM</td></tr><tr><th>Concealability</th><td>NA</td></tr><tr><th>Ammo</th><td>50</td></tr><tr><th>Mode</th><td>SA/BF</td></tr><tr><th>Damage</th><td>20D</td></tr><tr><th>Weight</th><td>1,200</td></tr><tr><th>Cost</th><td>600,000¥</td></tr></table><ul><li>Works like a vehicle laser (the Ares Firelance): Power −2 at medium range, −4 at long, −6 at extreme.</li>\n<li>Antivehicle: vehicles don't automatically stage the Damage Level down, and only half the vehicle's Armor (round down) reduces the Power.</li>\n<li>Ammo is shots before recharging: a full recharge takes 10 minutes; idle, it regains 1 shot per 4 Combat Turns with no firing (firing within three turns wastes the accumulated time).</li>\n<li>A rigger jacked into or directly controlling a vehicle or missile it hits takes Physical damage from ASIST backlash (as the Loral-Vought \"Zapper\", Rigger 2 p.94).</li>\n<li>Against other ships: <strong>9LN</strong>. Needs a medium or larger remote turret.</li></ul><p><em>Cyberpirates p.180.</em></p>"
      },
      "sort": 500000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1
      },
      "flags": {
        "sr2e-cyberpirates": {
          "source": {
            "page": 180,
            "cell": "AN/EDQ-12 ANDREWS stat block",
            "verified": "300dpi+visual"
          }
        }
      },
