    {
      "_id": "b07588709351c71a",
      "name": "Mk 197 MADCAP Torpedo",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>The most widely used torpedo of the era: up to 75 knots, an active sonar-seeker warhead as standard (passive sonar or thermal heads available). Launched by subs and surface ships, or dropped from anti-submarine helicopters.</p><table><tr><th>Handling</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Speed</th><td>115</td></tr><tr><th>Range</th><td>15 km</td></tr><tr><th>Body</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Signature</th><td>5/5</td></tr><tr><th>Intelligence</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Damage</th><td>14DN</td></tr><tr><th>Weight</th><td>750 kg</td></tr><tr><th>Cost</th><td>350,000¥</td></tr></table><ul><li>It activates on splashdown; range is measured from the splash point. Sonar Rating 1 for active-sonar range.</li><li>Wire-guided: a rigger on the sub controls it until the cable is cut, then its own Intelligence takes over. Helicopter-dropped MADCAPs have no wire and can't be rigged.</li></ul><p><em>Cyberpirates p.181.</em></p>"
      },
      "sort": 700000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1
      },
      "flags": {
        "sr2e-cyberpirates": {
          "source": {
            "page": 181,
            "cell": "Mk 197 MADCAP Torpedo stat block",
            "verified": "300dpi+visual"
          }
        }
      },
