    {
      "_id": "92d920a8e842713d",
      "name": "Torpedo Probe",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>A Mark 197 body carrying a sonar array instead of explosives: it reports other subs back to the mother ship over an optical cable.</p><table><tr><th>Handling</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Speed</th><td>150</td></tr><tr><th>Range</th><td>15 km (depth 750 meters)</td></tr><tr><th>Body</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Signature</th><td>5/3</td></tr><tr><th>Intelligence</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Damage</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Sonar</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Weight</th><td>950 kg</td></tr><tr><th>Cost</th><td>150,000¥</td></tr></table><p>Fixed speed 150 m per Combat Turn (about 100 knots); the cable limits it to 3 km (about 20 turns, a minute of recon). Steered from the sub by joystick, or by rigger link if the sub has a remote control deck.</p><p><em>Cyberpirates p.182.</em></p>"
      },
      "sort": 1000000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1
      },
      "flags": {
